<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('_head', { graph, pageTitle }) %>
</head>
<body class="cc-task-body">
  <main
    class="cc-task"
    data-deployment-stage1
    data-deployment-stage4a
    <%= deploymentAuthorityAvailable ? 'data-deployment-stage2a' : '' %>
    <%= deploymentVerificationAvailable ? 'data-deployment-stage2b' : '' %>
    <%= deploymentMutationAvailable ? 'data-deployment-stage3b' : '' %>
    <%= deploymentLifecycleAvailable ? 'data-deployment-stage5a' : '' %>
    <%= deploymentReauthorizationAvailable ? 'data-deployment-stage5b' : '' %>
  >
    <nav class="cc-task-nav">
      <a class="cc-link" href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>">Back to Studio</a>
      <span class="cc-draft-status">Working Version <%= revision %></span>
    </nav>

    <p class="cc-kicker">Deployment · qualification boundary</p>
    <h1>Prepare an exact Release and deployment target safely.</h1>
    <p class="cc-task__dek">
      Offline simulation remains available everywhere. Installed Windows HiVenues may also create a protected
      deployment-only SSH authority for provider handoff. HiVenues verifies an explicitly trusted SSH target
      without changing it first. In a qualified installed runtime, an exact immutable Release may then advance
      to a separate deployment consequence review before any server mutation. After a healthy deployment,
      Stage 4A can prepare a domain plan and exact DNS instructions locally. DNS changes, server host-routing,
      TLS issuance and provider payment remain held until a later explicit review.
    </p>

    <% if (error) { %>
      <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-error>
        <strong>Deployment simulation stopped</strong>
        <p><%= error %></p>
      </section>
    <% } %>

    <% if (!deploymentAvailable) { %>
      <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-unavailable>
        <h2>Local deployment simulation is unavailable</h2>
        <p>This runtime was not started with the Stage-1 deployment services.</p>
      </section>
    <% } else { %>
      <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-profile>
        <p class="cc-kicker">Target family</p>
        <h2>Offline synthetic target</h2>
        <p>This adapter exists only to qualify the product state machine before real infrastructure authority is admitted.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>Capabilities</summary>
          <p><code><%= deploymentProfile.capabilities.join(', ') %></code></p>
          <p>External effects: <strong><%= deploymentProfile.externalEffects ? 'enabled' : 'disabled' %></strong></p>
        </details>
        <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/targets">
          <button class="cc-button cc-button--ink" type="submit" data-create-deployment-target>Add offline deployment target</button>
        </form>
      </section>

      <% if (deploymentAuthorityAvailable) { %>
        <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-authority-profile style="margin-top:1.2rem">
          <p class="cc-kicker">Reference server handoff</p>
          <h2>Prepare a protected SSH deployment identity</h2>
          <p>
            HiVenues can generate a deployment-only key locally. The private key is protected by the
            operating system and is not shown here. Only the public key is handed to the server provider.
          </p>
          <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/targets/reference-ssh">
            <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-create-reference-ssh-target>Prepare server target</button>
          </form>
        </section>
      <% } %>

      <% if (!releases.length) { %>
        <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-no-release style="margin-top:1.2rem">
          <h2>Create a Release first</h2>
          <p>Deployment can use only an immutable HiVenues Release. Working state cannot be deployed.</p>
          <a class="cc-button" href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/release">Review and create a Release</a>
        </section>
      <% } %>

      <section style="margin-top:2rem">
        <p class="cc-kicker">Local targets</p>
        <h2>Deployment state</h2>

        <% if (!deployments.length) { %>
          <p data-deployment-empty>No deployment targets yet.</p>
        <% } %>

        <div class="cc-release-list">
          <% deployments.forEach((deployment) => { %>
            <article class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-record="<%= deployment.id %>">
              <div>
                <p class="cc-kicker"><%= deployment.providerKind === 'synthetic-offline' ? 'Synthetic target' : 'Server target' %></p>
                <h3><%= deployment.id %></h3>
                <p>
                  State:
                  <strong data-deployment-state><%= deployment.state %></strong>
                </p>
                <p>Provider: <%= deployment.providerKind %> · <%= deployment.providerProfile %></p>
                <p>Provider state: <%= deployment.providerState %> · Payment state: <%= deployment.paymentState %></p>
                <p>Health: <%= deployment.healthState %> · Rollback: <%= deployment.rollbackState %></p>

                <% if (deployment.authorityPublic) { %>
                  <section class="cc-consequence-card" data-deployment-authority-public>
                    <h4>Deployment public key</h4>
                    <p>
                      This public key may be supplied to the server provider. The protected private key remains
                      local to this HiVenues installation.
                    </p>
                    <label>
                      Public SSH key
                      <textarea
                        rows="5"
                        readonly
                        data-deployment-public-key
                      ><%= deployment.authorityPublic.publicKey %></textarea>
                    </label>
                    <p>Key fingerprint: <code data-deployment-public-key-fingerprint><%= deployment.authorityPublic.publicKeyFingerprint %></code></p>
                    <button
                      class="cc-button"
                      type="button"
                      data-copy-deployment-public-key
                    >Copy public key</button>
                    <span data-copy-deployment-public-key-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
                  </section>
                <% } %>

                <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server' && Object.keys(deployment.targetPublicFacts || {}).length) { %>
                  <p data-deployment-server-facts>
                    Server:
                    <code><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.username %>@<%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.host %>:<%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.port %></code>
                  </p>
                <% } %>

                <% if (deployment.selectedRelease) { %>
                  <p>
                    Selected Release:
                    <code data-selected-release><%= deployment.selectedRelease.id %></code>
                    · <code><%= deployment.selectedRelease.digest %></code>
                  </p>
                <% } %>

                <% if (deployment.package) { %>
                  <p>Prepared package: <code data-package-digest><%= deployment.package.packageDigest %></code></p>
                <% } %>

                <% if (deployment.activeRelease) { %>
                  <p>
                    Confirmed deployed Release:
                    <code data-active-release><%= deployment.activeRelease.id %></code>
                    · <code><%= deployment.activeRelease.digest %></code>
                  </p>
                <% } %>

                <% if (deployment.previousRelease) { %>
                  <p>Rollback candidate: <code data-previous-release><%= deployment.previousRelease.id %></code></p>
                <% } %>
              </div>

              <% if (
                deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                && deployment.activeRelease
                && ['healthy', 'rollback-available'].includes(deployment.state)
              ) { %>
                <section
                  class="cc-review-card"
                  style="margin-top:1rem"
                  data-domain-connection
                >
                  <p class="cc-kicker">Public address</p>
                  <% if (!deployment.publicEndpoint) { %>
                    <h4>Connect a domain</h4>
                    <p>
                      Choose the address people should eventually use for this deployed site.
                      HiVenues will prepare the exact DNS instructions first. Nothing on the Internet
                      or server changes in this step.
                    </p>
                    <form
                      method="post"
                      action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/domain/preflight"
                      data-domain-preflight-form
                    >
                      <label>
                        Domain name
                        <input
                          name="hostname"
                          required
                          autocomplete="off"
                          placeholder="dev.example.com"
                          data-domain-hostname
                        >
                      </label>
                      <button class="cc-button cc-button--ink" type="submit">Prepare domain setup</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } else { %>
                    <h4>Domain setup prepared</h4>
                    <p>
                      Planned public address:
                      <strong data-domain-hostname-value><%= deployment.publicEndpoint.hostname %></strong>
                    </p>

                    <% if (
                      deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-instructions-ready'
                      || deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-mismatch'
                    ) { %>
                      <p>
                        Next, these exact DNS records will need to point the domain at this deployment.
                        <strong>Nothing has been changed yet.</strong>
                      </p>
                      <dl data-domain-dns-instructions>
                        <% deployment.publicEndpoint.dns.requirements.forEach((record) => { %>
                          <div>
                            <dt><%= record.type %> record</dt>
                            <dd>
                              <code><%= record.name %></code>
                              →
                              <code><%= record.values.join(', ') %></code>
                            </dd>
                          </div>
                        <% }) %>
                      </dl>

                      <% if (deploymentPublicationExecutionAvailable) { %>
                        <section class="cc-review-card" style="margin-top:1rem" data-domain-dns-check>
                          <p class="cc-kicker">Guided DNS handoff</p>
                          <h5>Change only the record above at your DNS provider, then let HiVenues check it.</h5>
                          <p>
                            HiVenues does not receive registrar credentials and does not edit DNS in this flow.
                            The check below is read-only and must observe the exact prepared destination.
                          </p>
                          <form
                            method="post"
                            action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/domain/check"
                          >
                            <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-check-domain-dns>Check DNS</button>
                          </form>
                        </section>
                      <% } %>
                    <% } %>

                    <p data-domain-human-status>
                      <% if (deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-confirmed') { %>
                        Domain records confirmed. Secure connection is the next separate proof.
                      <% } else if (deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-mismatch') { %>
                        The last DNS check did not match the required destination.
                      <% } else { %>
                        DNS has not been checked yet.
                      <% } %>
                    </p>

                    <% if (
                      deploymentPublicationExecutionAvailable
                      && deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-confirmed'
                    ) { %>
                      <form
                        method="post"
                        action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/domain/check"
                        style="margin-top:.75rem"
                        data-domain-dns-recheck
                      >
                        <button class="cc-button" type="submit">Recheck DNS</button>
                      </form>
                    <% } %>

                    <% if (deployment.publicEndpoint.dns.observation) { %>
                      <details class="cc-review-card" style="margin-top:1rem" data-domain-dns-observation>
                        <summary>Last DNS observation</summary>
                        <p>Checked: <code><%= deployment.publicEndpoint.dns.observation.checkedAt %></code></p>
                        <p>Resolver: <code><%= deployment.publicEndpoint.dns.observation.resolver || 'system-dns' %></code></p>
                        <% deployment.publicEndpoint.dns.observation.records.forEach((record) => { %>
                          <p><code><%= record.type %> <%= record.name %> → <%= record.values.join(', ') %></code></p>
                        <% }) %>
                        <% if ((deployment.publicEndpoint.dns.observation.conflictingRecords || []).length) { %>
                          <p><strong>Conflicting address-family records:</strong></p>
                          <% deployment.publicEndpoint.dns.observation.conflictingRecords.forEach((record) => { %>
                            <p><code><%= record.type %> <%= record.name %> → <%= record.values.join(', ') %></code></p>
                          <% }) %>
                        <% } %>
                      </details>
                    <% } %>

                    <% if (
                      deploymentPublicationExecutionAvailable
                      && deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-confirmed'
                      && ['ready-for-request', 'unconfigured', 'awaiting-dns'].includes(deployment.publicEndpoint.tls.state)
                    ) { %>
                      <section class="cc-consequence-card" style="margin-top:1rem" data-domain-publication-entry>
                        <p class="cc-kicker">Secure publication</p>
                        <h5>DNS is confirmed. Review the live server consequence before publishing.</h5>
                        <p>
                          This next review does not change the server. It re-proves the restricted publication
                          capability and exact deployed Release before offering the bounded hostname action.
                        </p>
                        <a
                          class="cc-button cc-button--ink"
                          href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/publication-review"
                          data-review-live-publication
                        >Review secure publication</a>
                      </section>
                    <% } %>

                    <% if (
                      deploymentPublicationExecutionAvailable
                      && deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-confirmed'
                      && ['requesting', 'verified', 'degraded'].includes(deployment.publicEndpoint.tls.state)
                      && deployment.publicEndpoint.publicReadBack.state !== 'verified'
                    ) { %>
                      <section class="cc-review-card" style="margin-top:1rem" data-domain-public-verification>
                        <p class="cc-kicker">HTTPS proof</p>
                        <h5>Verify the certificate and exact public Release.</h5>
                        <p>
                          HiVenues will independently inspect TLS and then read the exact public health endpoint.
                          A generic successful page is not enough.
                        </p>
                        <form
                          method="post"
                          action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/publication-verify"
                        >
                          <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-verify-public-https>
                            Verify secure site
                          </button>
                        </form>
                      </section>
                    <% } %>

                    <% if (deployment.publicEndpoint.tls.state === 'verified') { %>
                      <p data-domain-tls-verified>
                        TLS certificate: <strong>verified</strong>.
                      </p>
                    <% } %>

                    <% if (deployment.publicEndpoint.publicReadBack.state === 'verified') { %>
                      <section class="cc-consequence-card" style="margin-top:1rem" data-public-readback-verified>
                        <p class="cc-kicker">Public proof complete</p>
                        <h5>Live HTTPS exact Release confirmed.</h5>
                        <p>
                          <code>https://<%= deployment.publicEndpoint.hostname %>/__hivenues/health</code>
                          returned the exact active runtime and immutable Release recorded by Studio.
                        </p>
                      </section>
                    <% } else if (deployment.publicEndpoint.publicReadBack.state === 'mismatch') { %>
                      <section class="cc-consequence-card" style="margin-top:1rem" data-public-readback-mismatch>
                        <h5>Public site identity does not match the expected Release.</h5>
                        <p>
                          HiVenues will not mark publication complete. Mismatched fields:
                          <code><%= deployment.publicEndpoint.publicReadBack.mismatchFields.join(', ') %></code>
                        </p>
                      </section>
                    <% } %>

                    <% if (
                      deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                      && deploymentPublicationInspectionAvailable
                      && deployment.activeRelease
                    ) { %>
                      <section
                        class="cc-review-card"
                        style="margin-top:1rem"
                        data-publication-capability-check
                      >
                        <p class="cc-kicker">Server readiness</p>
                        <h5>Check whether this server is ready to publish the domain securely.</h5>
                        <p>
                          This is a read-only check over the already trusted deployment connection.
                          It does not change DNS, Caddy, the firewall, TLS, the deployed Release, or server authority.
                        </p>
                        <a
                          class="cc-button"
                          href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/publication-capability"
                          data-check-publication-capability
                        >Check server readiness</a>
                      </section>
                    <% } %>

                    <% if (
                      deployment.publicationReview
                      && deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState !== 'dns-confirmed'
                    ) { %>
                      <details data-domain-consequence-review>
                        <summary>Review what a later live connection would do</summary>
                        <p>
                          The following are planned consequences only. This Stage-4A screen does not execute them.
                        </p>
                        <ol>
                          <% deployment.publicationReview.consequences.forEach((item) => { %>
                            <li><code><%= item %></code></li>
                          <% }) %>
                        </ol>
                        <p>Still held:</p>
                        <ul>
                          <% deployment.publicationReview.held.forEach((item) => { %>
                            <li><code><%= item %></code></li>
                          <% }) %>
                        </ul>
                      </details>
                    <% } %>

                    <% if (
                      deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-instructions-ready'
                      || deployment.publicEndpoint.domainState === 'dns-mismatch'
                    ) { %>
                      <details>
                        <summary>Change the planned domain</summary>
                        <form
                          method="post"
                          action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/domain/preflight"
                        >
                          <label>
                            Domain name
                            <input
                              name="hostname"
                              required
                              autocomplete="off"
                              value="<%= deployment.publicEndpoint.hostname %>"
                            >
                          </label>
                          <button class="cc-button" type="submit">Update domain plan</button>
                        </form>
                      </details>
                    <% } %>
                  <% } %>
                </section>
              <% } %>

              <% if (
                deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                && deployment.state === 'disconnected'
                && deploymentReauthorizationAvailable
              ) { %>
                <section class="cc-consequence-card" style="margin-top:1rem" data-reauthorization-entry>
                  <p class="cc-kicker">Deployment management</p>
                  <h4>Reconnect HiVenues to this preserved server without taking the site down</h4>
                  <p>
                    This creates a fresh deployment-only SSH authority locally. It does not change the server,
                    runtime, Release, DNS or TLS. Afterward HiVenues will show the exact public key that must be
                    restored temporarily to the original bootstrap account before any reviewed server consequence.
                  </p>
                  <form
                    method="post"
                    action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/reauthorization/prepare"
                  >
                    <button class="cc-button cc-button--ink" type="submit" data-prepare-reauthorization>
                      Prepare management reconnection
                    </button>
                  </form>
                </section>
              <% } %>

              <% if (
                deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                && deployment.state === 'reauthorizing'
                && deploymentReauthorizationAvailable
              ) { %>
                <section class="cc-consequence-card" style="margin-top:1rem" data-reauthorization-prepared>
                  <p class="cc-kicker">Temporary bootstrap handoff</p>
                  <h4>Restore the exact public key above to <code><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.bootstrapUsername %></code> only when ready</h4>
                  <p>
                    Use the server provider's out-of-band console to place only this newly generated public key
                    in the original bootstrap account's <code>authorized_keys</code>. Do not add it to
                    <code>hivenues-deploy</code> manually and do not change Caddy, the firewall, TLS, runtime or Release.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    HiVenues will first perform a read-only proof of the exact preserved server, runtime, Release
                    and publication state. The later reviewed consequence installs only this key for
                    <code>hivenues-deploy</code>, proves that login, removes the same temporary key from
                    <code><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.bootstrapUsername %></code>, and re-proves the public site.
                  </p>
                  <a
                    class="cc-button cc-button--ink"
                    href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/reauthorization-review"
                    data-review-reauthorization
                  >Review management reconnection</a>
                </section>
              <% } %>

              <% if (!['disconnected', 'reauthorizing'].includes(deployment.state)) { %>
                <div style="display:grid;gap:.8rem;margin-top:1rem">
                  <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server' && ['target-draft', 'awaiting-provider'].includes(deployment.state)) { %>
                    <form
                      method="post"
                      action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/connection"
                      data-deployment-server-connection
                    >
                      <label>
                        Server address
                        <input name="host" required autocomplete="off" inputmode="url" placeholder="server.example.com or IP address">
                      </label>
                      <label>
                        SSH port
                        <input name="port" required type="number" min="1" max="65535" value="22">
                      </label>
                      <label>
                        Remote account
                        <input name="username" required autocomplete="off" value="root">
                      </label>
                      <button class="cc-button" type="submit">Save public server details</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (
                    releases.length
                    && !(
                      (deployment.state === 'deploying' && deployment.stateReason === 'rollback-started')
                      || (
                        deployment.state === 'degraded'
                        && ['rollback-failed', 'authority-disconnect-removal-started'].includes(
                          deployment.stateReason
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  ) { %>
                    <form
                      method="post"
                      action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/release"
                      data-select-deployment-release
                    >
                      <label>
                        Immutable Release
                        <select name="releaseId" required>
                          <option value="">Choose Release</option>
                          <% releases.slice().reverse().forEach((item) => { %>
                            <option
                              value="<%= item.id %>"
                              <%= deployment.selectedRelease && deployment.selectedRelease.id === item.id ? 'selected' : '' %>
                            >
                              Version <%= item.draftRevision %><%= item.kind === 'urgent' ? ' + urgent update' : '' %> · <%= item.id %>
                            </option>
                          <% }) %>
                        </select>
                      </label>
                      <button class="cc-button" type="submit">Prepare exact Release package</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'synthetic-offline' && (deployment.state === 'target-draft' || deployment.state === 'awaiting-provider')) { %>
                    <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/target-ready">
                      <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-mark-target-ready>Simulate provider handoff</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'synthetic-offline' && (deployment.state === 'target-ready' || deployment.state === 'degraded' || deployment.state === 'unreachable')) { %>
                    <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/verify">
                      <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-verify-deployment-target>Verify synthetic target</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (
                    deployment.providerKind === 'synthetic-offline'
                    && deployment.selectedRelease
                    && deployment.package
                    && ['bootstrap-ready', 'healthy', 'rollback-available', 'degraded'].includes(deployment.state)
                  ) { %>
                    <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/deploy">
                      <button class="cc-button cc-button--ink" type="submit" data-deploy-release>Simulate exact Release deployment</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'synthetic-offline' && (deployment.state === 'healthy' || deployment.state === 'rollback-available')) { %>
                    <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/degrade">
                      <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-degrade-deployment>Simulate degraded health</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'synthetic-offline' && deployment.previousRelease && ['rollback-available', 'healthy', 'degraded'].includes(deployment.state)) { %>
                    <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/rollback">
                      <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-rollback-deployment>Simulate rollback</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (
                    deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                    && ['target-ready', 'degraded', 'unreachable'].includes(deployment.state)
                  ) { %>
                    <% if (deploymentVerificationAvailable) { %>
                      <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-ssh-verification>
                        <% if (deployment.targetPublicFacts.trustedHostKeyFingerprint) { %>
                          <strong>Retry read-only server verification</strong>
                          <p>
                            HiVenues will re-observe the server's SSH host fingerprint and require an exact match
                            with the trusted fingerprint before authenticating and repeating the read-only inspection.
                            No server changes are made by this retry.
                          </p>
                        <% } else { %>
                          <strong>Verify this server without changing it</strong>
                          <p>
                            HiVenues will first observe the server's SSH host fingerprint. It will not authenticate
                            until you explicitly accept that exact fingerprint.
                          </p>
                        <% } %>
                        <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/verify">
                          <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-observe-deployment-host-key>
                            <%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.trustedHostKeyFingerprint
                              ? 'Retry read-only verification'
                              : 'Observe server fingerprint' %>
                          </button>
                        </form>
                      </section>
                    <% } else { %>
                      <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-ssh-verification-held>
                        <strong>Server details ready for verification</strong>
                        <p>Read-only SSH inspection is not enabled in this runtime.</p>
                      </section>
                    <% } %>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server' && deployment.state === 'host-key-review') { %>
                    <section class="cc-consequence-card" data-deployment-host-key-review>
                      <h4>Review the SSH host fingerprint</h4>
                      <% if (
                        deployment.targetPublicFacts.trustedHostKeyFingerprint
                        && deployment.targetPublicFacts.trustedHostKeyFingerprint
                          !== deployment.targetPublicFacts.observedHostKeyFingerprint
                      ) { %>
                        <p>
                          <strong>The server fingerprint changed.</strong>
                          HiVenues will not authenticate until you explicitly trust the newly observed fingerprint.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                          Previously trusted:
                          <code data-deployment-trusted-host-fingerprint><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.trustedHostKeyFingerprint %></code>
                        </p>
                      <% } else { %>
                        <p>
                          First connection: compare this fingerprint with the value supplied by your server provider
                          or another trusted channel before continuing.
                        </p>
                      <% } %>
                      <p>
                        Observed:
                        <code data-deployment-observed-host-fingerprint><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.observedHostKeyFingerprint %></code>
                      </p>
                      <form
                        method="post"
                        action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/host-key/accept"
                      >
                        <input
                          type="hidden"
                          name="fingerprint"
                          value="<%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.observedHostKeyFingerprint %>"
                        >
                        <button class="cc-button cc-button--ink" type="submit" data-accept-deployment-host-key>
                          Trust this exact fingerprint
                        </button>
                      </form>
                    </section>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server' && deployment.state === 'bootstrap-ready') { %>
                    <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-readonly-verified>
                      <strong>Read-only server verification passed</strong>
                      <p>
                        <span>OS: <code data-deployment-verified-os><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedOs %></code></span>
                        ·
                        <span>Architecture: <code data-deployment-verified-architecture><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedArchitecture %></code></span>
                      </p>
                      <p>
                        <span>Memory: <code data-deployment-verified-memory><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedMemoryMb %> MB</code></span>
                        ·
                        <span>Disk: <code data-deployment-verified-disk><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedDiskMb %> MB</code></span>
                      </p>
                      <p>
                        Host fingerprint:
                        <code data-deployment-trusted-host-fingerprint><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.trustedHostKeyFingerprint %></code>
                      </p>
                      <p>
                        Dedicated-target suitability:
                        <strong data-deployment-dedicated-target>verified</strong>
                        · Bootstrap root authority:
                        <strong data-deployment-bootstrap-root-ready><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedBootstrapRootReady ? 'verified' : 'unavailable' %></strong>
                        · Public TCP listeners:
                        <code><%= (deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedPublicTcpPorts || []).join(', ') || 'none' %></code>
                      </p>
                      <% if ((deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedRemediableBaselineTcpPorts || []).length) { %>
                        <p data-deployment-remediable-baseline>
                          Recognized clean-OS baseline listeners to be contained by the bounded HiVenues firewall:
                          <code><%= deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedRemediableBaselineTcpPorts.join(', ') %></code>
                        </p>
                      <% } %>
                      <% if (!deploymentMutationAvailable) { %>
                        <p data-deployment-bootstrap-held>
                          Remote bootstrap remains held in this runtime.
                        </p>
                      <% } else { %>
                        <p>
                          Server mutation remains behind a separate exact consequence review. No DNS, TLS or
                          provider-payment action is included.
                        </p>
                      <% } %>
                    </section>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (
                    deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                    && deploymentMutationAvailable
                    && deployment.selectedRelease
                    && deployment.package
                    && deployment.state === 'degraded'
                  ) { %>
                    <section class="cc-review-card" data-deployment-readback-link>
                      <strong>Inspect the current deployed read-back without changing the server</strong>
                      <p>
                        Compare the live HiVenues runtime/Release provenance against the exact locally packaged
                        expectation before authorizing another deployment attempt.
                      </p>
                      <a
                        class="cc-button"
                        href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/readback"
                        data-inspect-deployment-readback
                      >Inspect deployed read-back</a>
                    </section>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (
                    deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                    && deploymentMutationAvailable
                    && deployment.selectedRelease
                    && deployment.package
                    && (
                      deployment.activeRelease
                      || deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedDedicatedTarget === true
                    )
                    && ['bootstrap-ready', 'deploying', 'healthy', 'rollback-available', 'degraded'].includes(deployment.state)
                    && !(deployment.state === 'deploying' && deployment.stateReason === 'rollback-started')
                    && !(
                      deployment.state === 'degraded'
                      && ['rollback-failed', 'authority-disconnect-removal-started'].includes(
                        deployment.stateReason
                      )
                    )
                  ) { %>
                    <section class="cc-consequence-card" data-deployment-consequence-review>
                      <strong>
                        <%= deployment.state === 'deploying'
                          ? 'Interrupted deployment can be resumed safely'
                          : 'Exact Release is ready for deployment consequence review' %>
                      </strong>
                      <p>
                        Review the trusted server identity, exact immutable Release, installed-runtime source
                        provenance and bounded server changes before HiVenues is allowed to mutate the target.
                      </p>
                      <a
                        class="cc-button cc-button--ink"
                        href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/review"
                        data-review-exact-deployment
                      >
                        <%= deployment.state === 'deploying' ? 'Review and resume exact deployment' : 'Review exact deployment' %>
                      </a>
                    </section>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (
                    deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                    && deployment.state === 'degraded'
                    && deployment.stateReason === 'ssh-target-suitability-conflict'
                  ) { %>
                    <section class="cc-consequence-card" data-deployment-target-conflict>
                      <strong>This server is not safe for a first HiVenues bootstrap.</strong>
                      <p>
                        Read-only inspection found an existing public listener or service that the Stage-3
                        Caddy/firewall bootstrap could disrupt. HiVenues will not expose the mutation review
                        for this target. Use a clean dedicated reference server instead.
                      </p>
                      <p>
                        Public TCP listeners:
                        <code data-deployment-conflict-ports><%= (deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedPublicTcpPorts || []).join(', ') || 'none' %></code>
                      </p>
                      <p>
                        Conflicts:
                        <code data-deployment-conflicts><%= (deployment.targetPublicFacts.verifiedTargetConflicts || []).join(', ') %></code>
                      </p>
                    </section>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (
                    deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                    && deploymentLifecycleAvailable
                    && deployment.previousRelease
                    && deployment.publicEndpoint
                    && deployment.publicEndpoint.publicReadBack.state === 'verified'
                    && (
                      ['rollback-available', 'healthy'].includes(deployment.state)
                      || (deployment.state === 'deploying' && deployment.stateReason === 'rollback-started')
                      || (deployment.state === 'degraded' && deployment.stateReason === 'rollback-failed')
                    )
                  ) { %>
                    <section class="cc-consequence-card" data-real-rollback-entry>
                      <p class="cc-kicker">Release rollback</p>
                      <h4>
                        <%= deployment.stateReason === 'rollback-failed'
                          || deployment.stateReason === 'rollback-started'
                          ? 'Review and recover the interrupted rollback'
                          : 'A previous exact Release is available' %>
                      </h4>
                      <p>
                        Current public Release:
                        <code><%= deployment.activeRelease.id %></code>.
                        Rollback candidate:
                        <code><%= deployment.previousRelease.id %></code>.
                        HiVenues will preserve the qualified runtime and must re-prove the public site afterward.
                      </p>
                      <a
                        class="cc-button cc-button--ink"
                        href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/rollback-review"
                        data-review-real-rollback
                      >Review exact rollback</a>
                    </section>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (
                    deployment.providerKind === 'ssh-server'
                    && deploymentLifecycleAvailable
                    && deployment.activeRelease
                    && deployment.publicEndpoint
                    && (
                      (
                        ['healthy', 'rollback-available'].includes(deployment.state)
                        && deployment.publicEndpoint.publicReadBack.state === 'verified'
                      )
                      || (
                        deployment.state === 'degraded'
                        && deployment.stateReason === 'authority-disconnect-removal-started'
                        && ['removal-started', 'remote-removed'].includes(
                          deployment.targetPublicFacts.authorityDisconnectState
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  ) { %>
                    <section class="cc-review-card" data-real-disconnect-entry>
                      <p class="cc-kicker">Deployment authority</p>
                      <h4>
                        <%= deployment.stateReason === 'authority-disconnect-removal-started'
                          ? 'Finish the interrupted authority disconnect'
                          : 'Disconnect HiVenues management without taking the site down' %>
                      </h4>
                      <p>
                        This is not a site deletion. The review removes only the exact HiVenues deployment key
                        from the steady server account, proves that key can no longer authenticate, revokes the
                        local protected private key, and preserves the running site plus local host/Release history.
                      </p>
                      <a
                        class="cc-button"
                        href="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/disconnect-review"
                        data-review-real-disconnect
                      >Review authority disconnect</a>
                    </section>
                  <% } %>

                  <% if (deployment.providerKind === 'synthetic-offline') { %>
                    <form method="post" action="/hivenues/studio/<%= graph.identity.slug %>/deploy/<%= deployment.id %>/disconnect">
                      <button class="cc-button" type="submit" data-disconnect-deployment>Disconnect local target</button>
                    </form>
                  <% } else if (!deploymentLifecycleAvailable) { %>
                    <p data-real-disconnect-held>
                      Real deployment disconnect remains behind the installed lifecycle qualification gate.
                    </p>
                  <% } %>
                </div>
              <% } %>

              <details style="margin-top:1rem">
                <summary>State history</summary>
                <ol>
                  <% deployment.history.forEach((item) => { %>
                    <li><code><%= item.from || 'none' %> → <%= item.to %></code> · <%= item.at %></li>
                  <% }) %>
                </ol>
              </details>
            </article>
          <% }) %>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="cc-consequence-card" style="margin-top:2rem" data-deployment-stage1-boundary>
        <h2>Authority boundary</h2>
        <p>
          Synthetic deployment remains local-only. Protected SSH targets require explicit host-fingerprint trust
          and fixed read-only inspection before mutation is even reviewable. A qualified installed runtime may
          perform only the exact reviewed Stage-3B bootstrap/Release consequence. Stage 4A may now save a local
          domain plan and show exact DNS instructions, but provider payment, DNS mutation, server host-routing and
          TLS issuance remain outside this action.
        </p>
      </section>
    <% } %>
  </main>
  <script defer src="/js/hivenues-deployment.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
